  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Advisory until it is not",
      "items": [
        "Most of AGENTS.md is advice; the blocked list is deterministic, on every session, for everyone",
        "Two guards share one definition with their git hook, so a session and a bare git command cannot disagree"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Four layers, because each has a hole",
      "items": [
        "The commit guard checks the branch you stand on, which says nothing about where a push lands",
        "Every local hook is escapable; branch protection is the only layer that holds, and it is not a file in this repo"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "What is standardised",
      "items": [
        "Testing: 5 layers, 3 tools — a route being reachable is an E2E question, never a unit one",
        "Versions: 4 numbers, 4 owners — EAS owns the build numbers, fingerprint owns runtimeVersion"
      ]
    }
  ]
